advanced-open-on-startup = Automatically open Yapfast when your computer starts up
advanced-start-minimized = Start Yapfast minimized
advanced-start-minimized-description = Start Yapfast in the background, out of your way.
advanced-discord-links = Open Discord links in Yapfast
advanced-discord-links-description = discord:// links from other apps and shortcuts open here instead of Discord. Turning it off gives them back to the app that had them.
advanced-close-to-tray = Close to tray
advanced-close-to-tray-description = Closing the window keeps Yapfast running in the system tray, with any call. Quit from the tray icon's menu.
advanced-no-tray-description = No system tray is running, so closing the window quits Yapfast.
advanced-multiple-windows = Allow multiple windows
advanced-multiple-windows-description = Starting Yapfast while it runs opens another Yapfast, with its own window and tray icon. Off, it brings the open window forward.
advanced-gpu-rendering = Render with the GPU
advanced-gpu-rendering-description = Hardware acceleration. Off, Yapfast draws on the processor, which uses about half the memory.
advanced-gpu-encoding = Encode streams with the GPU
advanced-gpu-encoding-description = Screen sharing uses the graphics card's video encoder, which takes almost no processor time and looks better at low bitrates. Off, or without one, Yapfast encodes on the processor.
advanced-developer-mode = Developer Mode
advanced-developer-mode-description = Menus offer Copy ID for servers, channels and people, which helps when you write apps that use the Discord API.
advanced-icon-credits = Icons from Solar by 480 Design (CC BY 4.0), many of them adapted, and from Lucide (ISC).
advanced-restart-for-gpu = Yapfast switches to the GPU when it restarts. Restarting leaves any call.
advanced-restart-for-cpu = Yapfast switches to the processor when it restarts. Restarting leaves any call.
advanced-restart = Restart Yapfast
